  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I have an UN_TOKENIZED Lucene index called SENTID which contains, amongst many others, values like 'GHS02' and 'GHS04'. These can be readily searched with the query format SENTCODE:GHS02, but the truncated search SENTCODE:GHS* will not hit them.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Gert Schmeltz Pedersen explained to me last year, that this is due to the fact that all UN_TOKENIZED field queries are subjected to KeywordAnalyzer, which apparently casts your query to lowercase when truncation is used (note, though, that specifying the query as SENTCODE:ghs* does not solve the problem...).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Gert  promised to look into this, and possibly solve it by allowing configuration of other analyzers for specific UN_TOKENIZED fields. This has not been done in 2.4.1, though, unless I completely missed something.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For the time being, I work around this by creating both an uppercase and a lowercase entry for each occurrence of this field. A more general solution would be most welcome.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
  "duedate": null,
